 **Partition.** `emit-manifest` splits the scope file list into disjoint near-even parts in manifest order, each a complete manifest: own file part, full rubric (`rules`, `sections`), own digest, and `n_a` **plus, for every rule and section id, the out-of-part predicate (`NA_PREDICATES.outOfPart`)** — the only truthful status for an id whose evidence that part does not hold. Each part is a whole manifest over its own subset, so `validate-ledger` accepts it unchanged.
 
-**Union property, checked before merge.** The orchestrator checks these by hand, over every part manifest and its validated ledger: (a) the parts' file ids are disjoint and union to exactly that reviewer's file list; (b) `rules`/`sections` are equal in every part; (c) no rule or section id is `n/a` under the out-of-part predicate in **every** part — that means nobody reviewed it. An id `n/a` under a standing predicate may be `n/a` in every part and never blocks the merge; a part holding no evidence for an id records that truthful `n/a`, never a vacuous `pass`. Any check failing blocks the merge — that reviewer counts as incomplete. Across reviewers, the internal reviewers' lists union to the scope file list; `emit-manifest` checks this before writing any manifest (`assertReviewerUnion`) and fails otherwise.
+**Union property, checked before merge.** The orchestrator checks these by hand, over every part manifest and its validated ledger: (a) the parts' file ids are disjoint and union to exactly that reviewer's file list; (b) `rules`/`sections` are equal in every part; (c) no rule or section id is `n/a` under the out-of-part predicate in **every** part — that means nobody reviewed it. An id `n/a` under a standing predicate may be `n/a` in every part and never blocks the merge; a part holding no evidence for an id records that truthful `n/a`, never a vacuous `pass`. Any check failing blocks the merge — that reviewer counts as incomplete. Across reviewers, the internal reviewers' lists cover the scope file list; `reviewerFiles` guarantees it (only impl-review Testing narrows).
 
 **One fresh dispatch per part** ("Clean-context review iteration" holds verbatim). A part interrupted twice escalates to the user; the split is never applied recursively.
 
